# LNDL Luxe — Cardamom Chiaroscuro Nocturne — DHP 2025 Stock-Corrected Control V8

## Authority and status

**Date:** 2026-09-02
**Concentration:** 20% EdP; 6,000 uL concentrate + 24.00 mL ethanol 96%
**Family:** nocturnal cardamom-lavender soft amber / aromatic LNDL control
**Predecessor:** `formulas/LNDL_Luxe_Cardamom_Chiaroscuro_Nocturne_DHP2025_Interiorized_V6_30mL_20pct_Development.md`, working-tree SHA-256 `DB60DA30D6F5EBE6935CB2C24FD9D750B83D727759552D246724216CB141015A`
**Status / claim ceiling:** `DESIGN HYPOTHESIS / COMPUTATIONAL / NOT TESTED / HOLD`. `NO COMPOUNDING`, `NO PROCUREMENT`, `NO SAFETY OR STABILITY CLEARANCE`, `NO PERFORMANCE CLAIM`, and `NO RELEASE`.

Rejected `formulas/LNDL_Luxe_Cardamom_Chiaroscuro_Nocturne_DHP2025_CarawayRestored_V7_30mL_20pct_Development.md` remains `USER-REJECTED DESIGN / CLARITY` provenance and is not the family control. V8 derives only from accepted Interiorized V6.

## Target identity

This control preserves V6's cold green cardamom capsule, restrained lavender hinge, warm crushed-seed interior, violet-suede complexion, literal cedar/vetiver silhouette, and creamy coumarinic skin recurrence. The sole stock correction removes depleted Polysantol from execution. A whole-use Ebanol stock provides only a bounded yielding-wood comparator; it is not called a chemical, sensory, temporal, or safety equivalent.

Reject/HOLD if physical evaluation finds cardamom loss, lavender detergent, culinary spice, pastry, lipstick iris, explicit leather, generic amberwood, or a detached Ebanol sandal note.

