## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

**Planes:** front capsule; inner pod shell; living lavender middle; crushed-seed chamber; violet cloth; cedar/vetiver rear; yielding inner wood; creamy skin echo.

| Window | Intended event | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| opening, 0-5 min | cardamom capsule and polished rind lead | NOT TESTED |
| top, 5-30 min | shell contracts through lavender into warm seed tissue | NOT TESTED |
| heart, 30-120 min | violet-suede cloth and hayed almond grow around seed | NOT TESTED |
| late heart, 2-6 h | cedar/vetiver verticality frames yielding wood | NOT TESTED |
| drydown, 6-24 h | coumarinic skin and pencil-root residue recall the pod | NOT TESTED |

**Textures:** polished; waxed; dry; cool; cineolic; fibrous; floral-herbal; airy; hayed; fatty; almond-grained; violet-cloth; suede-pressure; metallic; pencil-dry; earthy; rooty; yielding; creamy-lactonic.

**Transitions / recurrence:** rind→cardamom; cardamom→terpinyl shell; shell→lavender; lavender→Jessemal; Jessemal→coumarin; dried fruit→violet cloth; cloth→leaf-metal stitch; stitch→cedar; cedar→vetiver; vetiver→yielding wood; heliotropal/coumarin→Ethylene Brassylate. Pressure is dry spice, camphor and cedar; release is floral air, yielding wood and one skin musk. All are intended, not smelled.

