5. **VIOLET-SUEDE COMPLEXION:** Givaudan AIMI (200 uL), Irotyl (120 uL), Dihydro Beta Ionone (60 uL), Suederal (30 uL), Beta Ionone (20 uL), Alpha Ionone (10 uL), Orivone (10 uL).
6. **DEDICATED TRANSITION STITCHES:** Leafovert (20 uL), Dynascone (10 uL), Scentenal (10 uL).
7. **LITERAL CEDAR-VETIVER SILHOUETTE:** Cedarwood oil Virginia (200 uL), Cedarwood EO (645 uL), Vetiver EO (India) (290 uL), Vetikon (170 uL).
8. **EBANOL FUNCTIONAL-APPROXIMATION CHAMBER:** Ebanol (610 uL).
9. **SEED-TO-WOOD PRESSURE CONTOUR:** Kephalis (120 uL), Iso E Super (100 uL), Cashmeran (50 uL).
10. **QUIET ADHESION MATRIX:** Hexyl Salicylate (150 uL), Ethylene Brassylate (500 uL), Dipropylene Glycol (20 uL).
11. **ETHYLENE BRASSYLATE SKIN RECURRENCE:** Ethylene Brassylate (500 uL).
Reconcile 6,000 uL before 24.00 mL ethanol. Order is not safety, stability or maturation clearance.

## Controlled blinded test plan

First qualify the control using independently prepared V8-E and V8-0 constant-total samples. Use two independently prepared complete sets, anonymous codes, AB/BA order, equal application, and free description before scoring at 0, 5, 30, 120 minutes, 6 and 24 hours. Score LNDL recognition, cardamom, lavender hinge, yielding transition, cedar/vetiver, skin recurrence, overall liking, transition pleasure, drydown pleasure, re-smell desire, muddiness, harshness and Ebanol detachment. A null means no detected effect at this dose/protocol. Do not use rejected V7 as control.

